        "original_id": "88628065-79db-5246-ab31-af68257ce345",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Walton, John Wooden, Brad Nessler, Tom Tolbert\n- Organizations: UCLA Bruins, UCLA, ABC, NCAA\n- Events: 2003 NBA Finals\n- Topics: college basketball awards, national championships, sports broadcasting\n\nFacts:\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton became known for playing for John Wooden's UCLA Bruins.\n- Bill Walton won three consecutive College Player of the Year Awards while leading the UCLA Bruins to two NCAA Division I national titles.\n- John Wooden, nicknamed the \"Wizard of Westwood,\" won ten NCAA national championships in 12 years as UCLA's head coach, including a record seven straight titles.\n- The 2003 NBA Finals was broadcast on ABC in the United States.\n- Brad Nessler, Bill Walton, and Tom Tolbert served as the announcers for the ABC broadcast of the 2003 NBA Finals.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "757f35da-ca5d-58ef-a43d-d5a2f47a546c",
        "text": "Page: Bill Walton. Sentence: Walton became known playing for John Wooden's powerhouse UCLA Bruins in the early 1970s, winning three successive College Player of the Year Awards, while leading the Bruins to two Division I national titles.\nPage: John Wooden. Sentence: Nicknamed the \"Wizard of Westwood,\" he won ten NCAA national championships in a 12-year period as head coach at UCLA, including a record seven in a row.\nPage: 2003 NBA Finals. Sentence: The series was broadcast on U.S. television on ABC, with Brad Nessler, Bill Walton, and Tom Tolbert announcing.",
